        "why": "This clip puts the declaration in the scene of Moses asking to see God’s glory. The hosts explain that God makes his “goodness pass before” Moses and that the name must be accompanied by truth: “glory that doesn’t have truth to it can just go to the emotions.” They then read verses 6–7 and connect Yahweh’s name with covenant-keeping love.",
        "episodeTitle": "Exodus 33-34: Cleft of the Rock",
