        "startSec": 635,
        "endSec": 806,
        "why": "Stay with the immediate context and hear the passage read as the climax of Moses’ encounter in the rock. The discussion emphasizes the contrast between God’s protected, partial self-disclosure—“you shall see my back”—and the revealed name: “a God merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and abounding in steadfast love and faithfulness.”",
